    <item>
      <title>Anode-free zinc batteries enabled by structurally robust solid–electrolyte interphase</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01993-7</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Sustainability, Published online: 17 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01993-7"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01993-7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Zinc metal batteries are sustainable, but deep cycling triggers a catastrophic structural collapse of the solid–electrolyte interphase. By retaining trace reserved zinc during stripping, this work prevents solid–electrolyte interphase degradation, enabling a 99.96% Coulombic efficiency and stable anode-free pouch cells.</content:encoded>
